The order of making 1D/2D contour plots using Clarence scripts:

1. Make contour output root files

copy makeplots.sh to your project directory, modify the sbatch directives/script path/command run order/etc. accordingly;
run makeplots.sh --> output root files (example files are already included in the same dir as the scripts)

2. Make plots out of the files from 1

PLEASE USE ROOT6 when you make plots! ('module load root' should be okay on Cedar)

no need to submit jobs for this step since making plots is very fast;

check the input root file names in plot1d.sh and plot2d.sh before running them;

run 'source plot1d.sh' for 1D plots
run 'source plot2d.sh' for 2D plots
